  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A body of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> undergoes simple harmonic motion with a period <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span>. Which of the following expressions represents the magnitude of the restoring force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> acting on the body when its displacement from the equilibrium position is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2 \\pi m x}{T^2}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{4 \\pi^2 m x}{T^2}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{4 \\pi^2 m x}{T}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2 \\pi^2 m x}{T^2}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
